1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A real remote job can wait one extra day.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,200
A fake one cannot, which is why it shouts.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,800
This is a checklist. Not a crime drama. Not a guarantee you will get hired.

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:19,200
Flag one. They pay you to pay them. Equipment fees. training fees. software licenses.

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:24,000
A job that starts with your debit card is not onboarding. It is a storefront.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,400
Flag two. The company has no body. No real address. No working site. No named humans.

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:34,800
A logo in a Google Doc is not a company. It is clip art with ambition.

8
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:40,200
Flag three. There is no interview. Just a text. A form. An offer in twelve minutes.

9
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,400
Hiring is annoying. Scammers skip the annoying part because they are selling panic.

10
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:51,200
Flag four. A check arrives first. Then they ask you to buy gear and wire the rest back.

11
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,400
That check can bounce after you sent the cash. Banks are not a plot twist factory for fun.

12
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:03,000
Two-minute check. Search the exact company name plus the word careers. Open the official site yourself.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,200
Do not use the link they texted. Type the domain. Find a real person. Find a real listing.

14
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:15,200
If you already sent money, use official complaint channels. Do not pay a recovery expert who DMs you.

15
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:21,400
A real employer will survive a slow Tuesday. Save the card. Close the tab. Keep your selfie.
